In the nearly two-minute preview, the K-pop star plays Seo Mi-rae, a young woman who looks for love in a dating simulation service. As her impossibly perfect dates with various attractive partners in the virtual world — including meetups in a lavish palace, a college campus and private beach &#8212; complicate the connections she has in her real life, JISOO&#8217;s character asks, &#8220;Is there a perfect match for me somewhere in this world?&#8221;

&#8220;Seo Mi-rae is worn out by work. Love? It&#8217;s the last thing on her mind,&#8221; a description for the project reads. &#8220;But a virtual dating service sparks feelings — and maybe a real shot at romance.&#8221;

Boyfriend on Demand will premiere on Netflix on March 6. Also starring Seo In-guk, the series is one of the projects JISOO worked on during BLACKPINK&#8217;s recent break from band activities. The singer-actress also released solo EP Amortage &#8212; which peaked at No. 11 on Billboard &#8216;s Top Album Sales chart &#8212; and a collaboration with Zayn Malik titled &#8220;Eyes Closed&#8221; in 2025.

Now, JISOO and bandmates ROSÉ, LISA and JENNIE are back together, embarking on a global tour last summer. DEADLINE &#8212; the quartet&#8217;s first collection of songs since 2022&#8217;s Billboard 200 -topper Born Pink &#8212; will arrive on Feb. 27, with BLACKPINK unveiling the full tracklist a couple of weeks before the Boyfriend on Demand trailer dropped.

